-- title:
--   Lemma 4.5: the feedback controls (4.18) converge, $\hat a^n_t\to\hat a^\infty_t$ a.s.
-- statement:
--   Under the setup of Lemma 4.4, let $\hat a^n$ be the feedback controls built from the optimizers $a^n_t$ by
--   $$\hat a^n_0=a^n_0(0),\qquad\hat a^n_{t+1}=a^n_{t+1}(\hat a^n_0+\dots+\hat a^n_t),\quad t=0,\dots,N-2.\quad(4.18)$$
--   Then for $t=0,\dots,N-1$,
--   $$\hat a^n_t\to\hat a^\infty_t\quad\text{a.s.}\quad(4.19)$$
--
--   In the proof of Theorem 4.1 this gives continuity of the map sending the competitors' average achievement to the team's optimal effort.
--
--   **Formalization Note** $\hat a^n_t$ is the random variable obtained by evaluating the recursion (4.18) at $Y$. The dynamic-programming identification of $\hat a^n$ with the optimal solution of $\sup_{a\in\mathcal A}\mathbb E[J^n(\sum_ta_t)-\sum_tC_t(a_t)]$ (p.23) is a remark, not a hypothesis.
--
--   Differences from the source:
--   - encoding: n = 1, 2, …, ∞ → n : ℕ plus separate limit objects J^∞, a^∞; reason: Lean convention; same sequences.
--   - reading: "(J^n)′ is monotone w.r.t. n" → nondecreasing in n at every x > 0 and y, or nonincreasing in n at every x > 0 and y; reason: a monotone sequence of functions.
--   - reading: â^n = (â^n_1, …, â^n_{N−1}) given by the optimal solution, with â^n_0 = a^n_0(0) and (4.18) → â^n defined by the recursion (4.18) from the optimizers, indices 0, …, N − 1; reason: the printed index list omits â^n_0, which the next sentence defines; the lemma uses â^n only through (4.18).
--   - encoding: V_t from (4.10)–(4.11) → valueENN: the supremum over a ≥ 0 of the kernel conditional expectation of V_{t+1}(x + a) minus C_t(a), in [0, ∞]; value is its real part; reason: the supremum in [0, ∞] has no junk value; conditional expectations as in the kernel encoding.
--   - encoding: a_t(x) the optimizer for V_t(x) → any functions a_t(x, y) ≥ 0 attaining the supremum in (4.11) with a finite objective, for a.e. y, every t < N and x ≥ 0 (IsOptimizer); reason: the optimizer is unique (C_t strictly convex), so this covers the paper's optimizer without choosing it.
--   - encoding: periods k = 0, …, N − 1 with noises X_{k+1}, Y_{k+1}; F^Y_k = σ(Y_1, …, Y_k) → Lean coordinates X k, Y k (0-based); F^Y_k is generated by the k-prefix of the noise path (truncPath); reason: Lean convention; same instances.
--   - generalization: the standing model of §3/§4 also fixes the idiosyncratic noise X (independent of Y, X_1, …, X_N independent) and φ_k with (3.1) → no assumption on X or φ; reason: X and φ do not occur in the statement, which therefore specializes to the standing model.
--   - encoding: (3.6) of H Hypothesis, an inequality between random variables 'for all x ≥ 0, k' → almost surely, simultaneously for all x ≥ 0 and k (Bound36); reason: x ↦ J(x, y) is continuous on ℝ₊ (H Hypothesis (1)) and the costs C_k are C¹, so 'for each x, a.s.' and 'a.s., for all x' are the same condition; same instances.
-- source:
--   Zhou, Optimal relative performance criteria in mean field contribution games, SSRN 3742584 (Nov. 13, 2022), Lemma 4.5, p.23, (4.18)–(4.19)

import Mathlib
import Definitions.Def_RelPerfMFG_Setup
import Definitions.Def_RelPerfMFG_HHypothesis
import Definitions.Def_RelPerfMFG_ValueRecursion

open MeasureTheory ProbabilityTheory Filter Topology

namespace RelPerfMFG

/-- **Lemma 4.5**, Zhou, *Optimal relative performance criteria in mean field contribution
games*, SSRN 3742584 (Nov. 13, 2022), p.23. Under the setup of Lemma 4.4, with `âⁿ` given by
`âⁿ₀ = aⁿ₀(0)` and `âⁿ_{t+1} = aⁿ_{t+1}(âⁿ₀ + … + âⁿ_t)` for `t = 0, …, N − 2` (4.18), for
`t = 0, …, N − 1`, `âⁿ_t → â^∞_t` a.s. (4.19).

**Formalization Note.** Setup of Lemma 4.4 restated (see Lemmas 4.3–4.4). `âⁿ_t` is the
feedback recursion (4.18) built from the optimizers and evaluated at `Y` (`feedback`); the
dynamic-programming identification of `âⁿ` with the optimal solution of
`sup_{a∈𝒜} E[Jⁿ(Σ a_t) − Σ C_t(a_t)]` (p.23) is a remark of the paper, not a hypothesis. The
printed index list `(âⁿ₁, …, âⁿ_{N−1})` is read as `(âⁿ₀, …, âⁿ_{N−1})`. 0-based periods. -/
theorem lemma_4_5 {Ω : Type*} [MeasurableSpace Ω] {N e : ℕ}
    (μ : Measure Ω) [IsProbabilityMeasure μ] (Y : Ω → NoisePath N e) (hY : Measurable Y)
    (C : Fin N → ℝ → ℝ) (hC : IsCostS4 C)
    (J : ℕ → ℝ → NoisePath N e → ℝ) (Jinf : ℝ → NoisePath N e → ℝ)
    (hJ : ∀ n, HHypothesis μ Y C (J n)) (hJinf : HHypothesis μ Y C Jinf)
    (hunif : ∃ α ∈ Set.Ioo (0 : ℝ) 1, ∃ A : Ω → ℝ, IsAdmissibleBound μ A ∧
      (∀ n, Bound36 μ Y C (J n) α A) ∧ Bound36 μ Y C Jinf α A)
    (hconv : ∀ y, ∀ x : ℝ, 0 ≤ x → Tendsto (fun n => J n x y) atTop (𝓝 (Jinf x y)))
    (a : ℕ → ℕ → ℝ → NoisePath N e → ℝ) (ainf : ℕ → ℝ → NoisePath N e → ℝ)
    (ha : ∀ n, IsOptimizer μ Y C (J n) (a n)) (hainf : IsOptimizer μ Y C Jinf ainf)
    (hmono : (∀ y, ∀ x : ℝ, 0 < x → Monotone (fun n => rderiv (fun x => J n x y) x)) ∨
      (∀ y, ∀ x : ℝ, 0 < x → Antitone (fun n => rderiv (fun x => J n x y) x))) :
    ∀ᵐ ω ∂μ, ∀ t : ℕ, t < N →
      Tendsto (fun n => feedback (a n) t (Y ω)) atTop (𝓝 (feedback ainf t (Y ω))) := by sorry

end RelPerfMFG
